Membership can be withdrawn only after adoption of resolution in a meeting of Board of Directors. All such resolutions will be placed before the General Body for information. If the member has paid all the dues to the Society and cleared liability as sureties, if any, in full, he can withdraw his membership, provided that a member is required to give three month notice to the Board of Directors and give a written request, explaining his reasons for withdrawal. Withdrawal/Cessation of membership does not absolve the member from any financial or other liabilities he has as a member. 

